FAQ = [
 ("Does the 2023+ Pilot TrailSport need an aftermarket hitch?",
  "No. Honda's press kit lists a tow hitch as standard on the TrailSport, and Honda's Info Center describes it as an integrated Class III hitch. It sits behind the TrailSport's full-size spare tire. Every other trim (LX, Sport, EX-L, Touring, Elite, and the Black Edition from 2025) needs either Honda's dealer-installed towing accessories or an aftermarket hitch like the ones on this page."),
 ("How much can a 2023–2026 Pilot tow?",
  "Honda rates the Pilot at 3,500 lb with two-wheel drive and 5,000 lb with all-wheel drive. Honda also recommends premium fuel when towing more than 3,500 lb. A hitch rated at 6,000 lb doesn't change either number; you tow to whichever is lower, the hitch or the Pilot. The same goes for tongue weight: the trailer's tongue load plus anything in the receiver has to stay within both ratings."),
 ("Is a Class IV hitch worth it on a Pilot?",
  "Only for headroom on tongue weight. The Draw-Tite 76453 is a Class IV rated 6,000 lb GTW and 900 lb tongue weight, the same GTW as CURT's Class III 13472. The Pilot's own 5,000 lb limit doesn't move. The practical benefit is margin for a heavy hitch cargo carrier or a platform rack with e-bikes, where tongue load rises quickly."),
 ("Why does the Draw-Tite hitch exclude the full-size spare?",
  "Draw-Tite lists the 76453 for the 2023–2026 Pilot 'except w/Full Size Spare Tire.' The TrailSport is the trim with a standard full-size spare, and Honda mounts its standard hitch behind that spare. Since the TrailSport already has a hitch, this exclusion mainly matters if you added a full-size spare to another trim. Check under the rear before you order."),
 ("Will a hitch affect the hands-free power tailgate?",
  "CURT's fit notes for its 13472 hitch say Pilots with a hands-free liftgate need a factory sensor relocation kit. The budget hitches on this page are patterned on the 13472, so assume the same applies and ask the seller. Honda lists the hands-free power tailgate as available on higher trims, so check whether yours has it before you buy."),
 ("Do 2016–2022 Pilot hitches fit the 2023 Pilot?",
  "No. The fourth generation has a different body and rear structure. CURT's 13146, for example, is listed for the 2016–2022 Pilot and 2014–2020 MDX, while its 2023+ Pilot hitch is the 13472. Draw-Tite's 76453 also starts at 2023. Buy a hitch whose listing says 2023–2026 Pilot. That applies to wiring harnesses and ball mounts with vehicle-specific brackets too."),
 ("Does the Acura MDX hitch fit the Pilot?",
  "The 2022+ MDX and 2023+ Pilot share a platform, and both CURT (13472) and Draw-Tite (76453) list them together. Most budget hitches on Amazon also name both vehicles. Still, buy a listing that names the Pilot, since a listing that names only the MDX doesn't confirm the fit. That's why CURT's 13472 isn't linked here: its Amazon title names the MDX only."),
 ("Should I get Honda's dealer hitch or an aftermarket one?",
  "Honda sells towing accessories for dealer installation, and a dealer install keeps everything under Honda's accessory coverage and gets the wiring done at the same visit. Aftermarket hitches cost less and CURT and Draw-Tite publish their ratings and install notes. We couldn't verify a Honda part number and price for the 2023+ hitch, so ask your dealer for a quote to compare."),
 ("What wiring does a Pilot need?",
  "A hitch alone won't light a trailer. You need at least a 4-way flat connector for tail, brake and turn lights. A trailer with electric brakes also needs a 7-way connector and a brake controller. Ask your Honda dealer what the towing accessory kit includes, or buy a harness that names the 2023+ Pilot. Test every light function before the first trip."),
 ("Can I use a vertical bike rack on these hitches?",
  "CURT says its 13472 is not compatible with vertical-hanging bike racks, the kind that hang bikes from their front wheels in a tall mast. Budget copies of the 13472 may carry the same limit. Platform racks and standard hanging racks are fine within the tongue rating. If you already own a vertical rack, ask the seller before you buy."),
]

